<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8"?>
<!--
  SEO / crawlability note — READ BEFORE EDITING.

  This app is a client-rendered SPA that uses HASH-based routing (e.g.
  https://tresor-couture.vercel.app/#/shop). Search engines DROP everything
  after the '#' when crawling and indexing, so every hash URL collapses to the
  same document: the root "/". Listing "/#/shop", "/#/product/123", etc. in a
  sitemap therefore does NOT create distinct indexable pages — Google treats
  them as duplicates of "/". (The old #-fragment AJAX-crawling scheme was
  deprecated by Google in 2015 and is no longer supported.)

  There is also no server-side rendering or prerender step, and vercel.json
  only rewrites /auth/action -> /index.html (no SPA catch-all). So clean path
  URLs like /shop or /product/:id would 404 at the edge and cannot be listed
  here honestly either.

  As a result this sitemap intentionally lists ONLY the root URL, which is the
  one URL that returns real HTML and renders the full app.

  RECOMMENDATION to make category / product pages individually crawlable:
    1. Migrate routing from hash (#/shop) to the History API (clean paths
       like /shop, /product/:id). The custom RouterContext already inspects
       window.location, so this is a contained change.
    2. Add a Vercel SPA catch-all rewrite so deep links resolve:
         { "source": "/(.*)", "destination": "/index.html" }
       (placed AFTER the existing /auth/action and /__/ rewrites).
    3. Add prerendering / SSR for crawlers — e.g. Vercel's prerender, a
       static prerender of key routes (vite-plugin-ssr / react-snap), or
       a small Edge/serverless function that injects per-route <title>,
       meta description, canonical, and Product structured data (JSON-LD).
    4. Once the above land, regenerate this sitemap with the clean path URLs
       for the home, shop categories, customise, and each product.
-->
<urlset xmlns="http://www.sitemaps.org/schemas/sitemap/0.9">
  <url>
    <loc>https://tresor-couture.vercel.app/</loc>
    <changefreq>weekly</changefreq>
    <priority>1.0</priority>
  </url>
</urlset>
